  Check migrations for statements that lock tables, rewrite them or break
  running code.

  With no arguments, migrail finds the migrations in the repository and detects
  the migration tool. Pass migration files or directories to check only those,
  or - to read SQL from standard input.

  Usage
    migrail check [path]... | - [flags]

  Flags
        --ci                  CI mode: no color, links or spinners
                              unless forced
        --compact             print one line per finding
        --db-version string   PostgreSQL major version in production,
                              such as 16 (default: 12)
    -d, --dir string          project root to search for migrations
                              (default: the repository root)
        --fail-on string      exit with code 1 on findings at or above:
                              error, warning, notice or never (default
                              "error")
    -f, --format string       output format: pretty or json (default
                              "pretty")
        --framework string    migration tool to use instead of detecting
                              it: sqitch, atlas, prisma, drizzle, goose,
                              dbmate, golang-migrate, flyway, sql
    -q, --quiet               print only findings and the summary
    -r, --rule strings        only run these rules, by ID or slug
        --skip-rule strings   skip these rules, by ID or slug
    -v, --verbose             print each phase with its timing

  Global flags
        --ascii           use ASCII symbols instead of Unicode
        --color string    use color: auto, always or never (default "auto")
        --no-hyperlinks   don't print clickable file links
        --theme string    color theme: auto, dark, light or mono
                          (default "auto")
